30,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,I visited the station block’s bin house. It’s worse than the open pile! The smell is trapped inside and carries further.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that’s a worrying detail. I found our annual costs are thirty-four thousand yen, mostly for cleaning up open bags.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, thirty-four thousand yen is a lot for just bags. I checked the complaint log; eleven of fourteen entries came from the gate household.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, that log is just noise. I timed the supervised mornings: fifty minutes each, so we’d each do twenty a year.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@May, twenty hours is manageable, but I found the frontages are unequal. One house has a driveway blocking most of its width, making a rotation impossible there.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, a driveway blocking the space? That sounds like a real problem for moving it around. I hope we don’t get stuck there.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Asuka, that’s a serious constraint. I also found the ward subsidy covers forty percent, capped at ninety thousand yen, which helps but doesn’t cover everything.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, the subsidy helps, but the ledger shows we’re already bleeding money on cleanup. I also checked the residents’ meeting; nobody volunteered to turn away late bags.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, nobody volunteering is exactly why I need the truck time. If the window starts before we wake up, who actually enforces it?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, the truck arrives between seven forty and eight fifteen. A strict window means waking up before the rest of us. That’s a heavy burden.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@May, that’s terrifying! I don’t want to be the one waking up in the dark to guard the bins. It feels like a trap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand the fear. But the subsidy covers forty percent of a build, capped at ninety thousand yen. It’s a real help, though not a full solution.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the truck time is brutal, but the real issue is who enforces it. At the meeting, three people admitted they wouldn’t turn away late bags.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, so the enforcement is a lie. If nobody will turn bags away, the ""managed hours"" are just a suggestion. I need a plan that doesn’t rely on us being nice.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, you’re right. The filing clerk says a permanent build needs five signatures and four months. If we can’t agree on enforcement, we can’t even start the paperwork.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, four months is forever! And if the bin house smells worse, why build one? I just want the August smell to stop without waking up early.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I hear you. But the ledger shows we spend thirty-four thousand yen yearly just on cleanup. A proper structure might stop that bleeding, even if it takes time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, four months is long, but the station block’s minutes show they were arguing over a broken latch within two years. A permanent structure just creates new fights.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, new fights are better than old ones if they’re fair. I just need to know we aren’t signing up for endless, unpaid labor.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the minutes prove structures breed conflict. But the frontage measurements show one house is physically blocked. We can’t rotate there. We need a plan that respects that reality.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
