60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I’m scared of the smell and the early mornings. If we build a box, will it just trap the stink like the station block’s?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, the station block’s base couldn’t be hosed out, which caused the smell. If we ensure ours is washable, it might actually solve the August problem.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, a washable base is a start, but the minutes show they fought over sweeping inside. Who is going to do that daily chore here?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, I timed the supervised mornings: fifty minutes each. If we rotate, that’s twenty hours a year per house. Manageable, but only if the base is actually cleanable.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@May, twenty hours is fine, but the filing clerk says a permanent build needs five signatures and four months. If we can’t agree on the daily chores, we can’t even start the paperwork.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, I don’t want to sweep a smelly box every day! If the station block fought over a latch, we’ll fight over the mop. I just want the smell gone.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I hear you. But the ledger shows we spend thirty-four thousand yen yearly just on cleanup. A proper structure might stop that bleeding, even if it takes time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, the ledger is just the tip of the iceberg. The real cost is the social friction. If we build a box, we’re just moving the argument from the kerb to the doorstep.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, social friction is real, but so is the thirty-four thousand yen. If we don’t fix the source, we’re just paying for the mess forever.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, you’re right about the money. But the clerk’s four-month timeline and the driveway constraint mean a build is the only option that doesn’t leave one household stuck.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, but if the box traps the smell like the station block’s, I’m stuck with the stink anyway! I don’t want a permanent prison for the bins.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that’s a fair worry. But the station block’s base couldn’t be hosed out. If we specify a washable floor, we avoid that trap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, a washable floor is a nice idea, but the minutes show they still fought over who sweeps. We’d just be trading the smell for the chore.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, the minutes show they fought because the base was uncleanable. If we fix the floor, the chore is minimal. I’d rather do twenty hours of easy work than pay thirty-four thousand yen yearly.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, twenty hours is acceptable, but the driveway blocks rotation. A permanent build is the only way to stop the gate household from bearing the brunt.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I’m still scared of the smell. But if the floor is washable and we share the work, maybe it’s not a prison? I just want August to be bearable.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, exactly. A washable base and shared duties make it bearable. I’m ready to vote for the enclosed structure, provided we specify that floor.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Midori"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Midori: @Rin, exactly. A washable base and shared duties make it bearable. I’m ready to vote for the enclosed structure, provided we specify that floor.""}]}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, I’m in. If we fix the floor and share the sweeping, we avoid the station block’s trap. I’d rather have a fair fight than a silent grudge.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"@Midori, I’m in. Twenty hours of easy work beats thirty-four thousand yen in endless cleanup. I’ll vote for the enclosed structure, as long as the floor is actually washable.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Midori, I’m in. The driveway makes rotation impossible, and the log proves the gate household is already drowning. I vote for the enclosed structure, with a washable base.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
